  "source_challenges": [
    "Did-create existence and the if-so specNumber/impactType roles are all part of the unchanged question. A nonempty positive NewTS witness answers yes; no Boolean field is imposed merely because one could be added.",
    "The original implementation returns all impact types, but the unchanged English and KO ask new TS creation. NewTS is the exact original Enum for that operation, not an old-query truth criterion.",
    "Require a nonempty complete NewTS witness prospectively. An empty graph result cannot establish no creation or resolve an abstention/negative answer, and would leave this positive-witness candidate pending.",
    "The WID output initially says TS38.xxx; same Core WI/editor/title and successive original first-draft, endorsement and approval records establish the resulting TS38.291 number. Do not substitute mere topic/date similarity.",
    "Initial draft creation/presentation, requested endorsement, reported actual endorsement, requested approval and reported actual approval are distinct roles.",
    "The WID also takes TR38.848 and other WG decisions forward. No sole-cause or all-study-results/all-TS-content attribution is asserted.",
    "Original indexed CQ2 ordering is ImpactTypeASC/TRASC; KO sort metadata differs. Prospective singleton requested-pair condition is needed to neutralize these axes/default10 on this frozen case only.",
    "Every retained matching NewTS target must be the directly documented TS38.291 and a valid typed complete target. This does not certify unrelated manual CSV classifications or optional impactDescription/power claims."
  ],
